+**Formulas:**
+- Opacity correction: $src.a = 1 - (1 - src.a)^{\frac{stepScale}{0.5}}$ [S1, unofficial].
+- Front-to-back blending: $dst = (1 - dst.a) \times src + dst$ [S1, unofficial].
+
+**Parameters:**
+- `stepScale`: Float parameter used in opacity correction. Typical value not specified, but used as divisor in exponent [S1, unofficial].
+- `threshold`: `ivec2` defining the range of iso values (0-255) to render. Default from TransferFunction is `(0, 255)` [S1, unofficial].
+- `stepSize`: `vec3` defining the step size in each dimension [S1, unofficial].
+- `iterations`: `int` defining the maximum number of ray marching steps [S1, unofficial].
+
+**Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
+- Out of bounds: Ray position is checked against 1.0 in x, y, z. If any exceed 1.0, the loop breaks [S1, unofficial].
+- Early termination: Ray marching breaks if accumulated alpha $dst.a \ge 0.95$ [S1, unofficial].
+- Normal decoding assumes a spheremap transform, attributed to Cry Engine 3 and Martin Mittring [S1, unofficial].
+
